            "review_title": "Review at El Abed",
            "review_text": "Johnmango928\nEdmonton, Canada545 contributions\n0\nGood Food, Good Value, Terrible Wait Time\nOct 2023 • Solo\nThis restaurant is not difficult to find. One (north) side of the alley is the kitchen and the other (south) side is the seating area.\n\nI stood outside the restaurant at 11:50 am waiting for it to open at noon. One waiter saw me and opened the restaurant so I could sit down. I ordered the grilled lamb with a salad. \n\nThen things started going downhill - other customers started streaming in, and some 3-4 tables were served and food was finished. \n\nBy 12:45pm my grilled lamb finally arrived.\n\nI understand that it took time to fire up the charcoal grill, but not an hour. 3 pieces of lamb were thin and should not take more than several minutes to cook each side.\n\nYes the lamb was perfectly grilled. The total price (lamb plus salad) came to 25 dinars. So it was great value.\n\nI would have awarded 5 stars if not for the long wait. Will not return.\nRead more\nWritten October 4, 2023",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-11",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
